WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.507
"You!" Zann blurted out in surprise.

2
00:00:03.508 --> 00:00:05.959
His voice was louder than he'd intended.

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.610
He glanced nervously at the door, expecting Slib to burst in.

4
00:00:09.611 --> 00:00:13.163
"Don't worry, Zann, he can't hear you."

5
00:00:13.164 --> 00:00:15.782
The old woman dropped the bag she was holding.

6
00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:19.478
"This room is hidden from most people."

7
00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:22.795
"How do you know my name?" Zann demanded.

8
00:00:22.796 --> 00:00:27.496
Then he realized he knew hers too—at least he thought he did.

9
00:00:27.497 --> 00:00:31.612
Teplo had mentioned it once. "You're Wyssa, aren't you?"

10
00:00:31.613 --> 00:00:35.357
"That's what they call me, yes," Wyssa said.

11
00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:40.418
"Now take my hand, and I'll zap you out of the palace before you're noticed."

12
00:00:40.419 --> 00:00:47.094
"No!" Zann said. "Not until you tell me everything you know about how my parents disappeared!"

13
00:00:47.095 --> 00:00:53.694
Wyssa looked startled. "How did you—? Never mind," she interrupted herself.

14
00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:58.000
"I suppose the old man told you I was involved."

15
00:00:58.001 --> 00:01:01.145
"Huh?" Now it was Zann's turn to be startled.

16
00:01:01.146 --> 00:01:05.301
"What old man? Wait—are you talking about Boz?"

17
00:01:05.302 --> 00:01:13.428
"Who else?" Wyssa sighed. "He's been poking around these past few years. I know he must suspect me."

18
00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:19.860
Zann didn't know what to say. All this time he'd thought Boz was doing nothing to find Zann's parents.

19
00:01:19.861 --> 00:01:24.104
"I suppose you deserve to know what happened," Wyssa said.

20
00:01:24.105 --> 00:01:33.670
"It doesn't matter now anyway. It all began when a very demanding new customer sent me to pick up a scatter beast in Fardark."

21
00:01:33.671 --> 00:01:41.507
"Fardark?" Zann said. The name sounded vaguely familiar, though for a moment he couldn't remember where he'd heard it.

22
00:01:41.508 --> 00:01:47.683
Then it came back to him. He'd seen it in Boz's diary while he was reading about his parents' travels.

23
00:01:47.684 --> 00:01:50.749
Fardark was the name of another world!

24
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.993
"It should have been an ordinary errand," Wyssa went on.

25
00:01:54.994 --> 00:02:03.300
"But my customer insisted I return via a wormhole that was convenient for him—one near the university.

26
00:02:03.301 --> 00:02:07.212
Your parents happened to be entering at the same moment.

27
00:02:07.213 --> 00:02:15.303
The chaotic energy of the scatter beast turned what should have been a minor collision into an explosion of unstable magic.

28
00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:18.803
I tried to grab your parents, to pull them out with me.

29
00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:24.805
But I wasn't able to save them. They went spinning off course and became stuck between worlds."

30
00:02:24.806 --> 00:02:30.261
Once again Zann was speechless. His mind buzzed with questions.

31
00:02:30.262 --> 00:02:36.010
But before he could ask any of them, a zap of energy shot through the room, and Morb appeared.

32
00:02:36.011 --> 00:02:40.109
"There you are!" he said irritably, glaring at Wyssa.

33
00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:43.200
"What in the world are you doing in here?

34
00:02:43.201 --> 00:02:45.964
I don't like having to track you when I—"

35
00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:50.778
Morb stopped short as he noticed Zann. His eyes widened.

36
00:02:50.779 --> 00:02:54.521
"You!" he spat out.

37
00:02:54.522 --> 00:02:58.201
"Where are they taking us?" Gliss whispered.

38
00:02:58.202 --> 00:03:00.590
They had walked deep into the forest.

39
00:03:00.591 --> 00:03:03.210
Perda shrugged, glancing at their captors.

40
00:03:03.211 --> 00:03:07.307
There were about half a dozen of them, all with stern looks on their faces.

41
00:03:07.308 --> 00:03:10.259
None of them would tell Fala or the kids anything.

42
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.580
Perda had been ready to fight back against that Floating spell.

43
00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:18.104
But then she, Gliss, and Fala had Restrain spells placed on them.

44
00:03:18.105 --> 00:03:22.813
Perda looked down at her arms, which appeared to be stuck at her sides.

45
00:03:22.814 --> 00:03:26.744
They came to a clearing. Several dozen people were gathered there.

46
00:03:26.745 --> 00:03:29.787
As Fala looked around, her eyes lit up.

47
00:03:29.788 --> 00:03:31.583
"Shem!" she called.

48
00:03:31.584 --> 00:03:38.855
A man turned around. "Fala?" he exclaimed. "I can't believe you're here."

49
00:03:38.856 --> 00:03:41.939
"Well, you have these people to thank for it."

50
00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.640
Fala nodded toward the captors. "They grabbed us in the forest."

51
00:03:46.641 --> 00:03:57.184
Shem laughed. "You can remove the Restrain spells," he told the captors. "They're on our side."

52
00:03:57.185 --> 00:04:01.649
Perda shook her arms. "Who are these people?" she asked Fala.

53
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:05.246
"Don't worry," Fala said. "They're friends."

54
00:04:05.247 --> 00:04:10.861
Shem told Fala that he and his group had been among the people who'd marched on the palace that morning.

55
00:04:10.862 --> 00:04:16.112
Now they were hiding in the woods, trying to figure out how to fight back against Morb.

56
00:04:16.113 --> 00:04:19.367
"Fala can help us," Shem told the group.

57
00:04:19.368 --> 00:04:23.318
"She has powerful friends and much knowledge."

58
00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:27.854
As the adults started discussing possible plans, Perda stopped listening.

59
00:04:27.855 --> 00:04:36.002
"I thought Zann would have found us by now," she whispered to Gliss and Darb. "I hope he's okay."

60
00:04:36.003 --> 00:04:41.355
Zann stared at Morb, gripped by the fury and triumph in the evil man's eyes.

61
00:04:41.356 --> 00:04:47.194
As Morb touched his fingertips together and sparks flew, Zann quickly rubbed his hands together.

62
00:04:47.195 --> 00:04:48.843
"Zap!" he cried.

63
00:04:48.844 --> 00:04:50.320
Nothing happened.

64
00:04:50.321 --> 00:05:01.803
"Too late, boy," sneered Morb. "Even a clever Red like you can't fight a Dousing spell."

65
00:05:01.804 --> 00:05:08.755
Zann darted toward the exit. But at that moment, a troll stepped forward, blocking the doorway with its huge body.

66
00:05:08.756 --> 00:05:12.879
"Let me through!" Zann yelled, throwing himself at the troll.

67
00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.913
The troll grunted with surprise as Zann pounded on it with his fists.

68
00:05:16.914 --> 00:05:20.831
Then Zann saw a glint of silver. The talisman!

69
00:05:20.832 --> 00:05:28.976
He remembered Fala's words: If only we could get our hands on one of those talismans. It could be invaluable to us.

70
00:05:28.977 --> 00:05:32.422
Zann quickly grabbed the talisman and yanked it loose.

71
00:05:32.423 --> 00:05:34.333
"Get him!" Morb yelled.

72
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:39.869
The troll reached down. Zann barely managed to slip free of the creature's grasp.

73
00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.925
He stuck the talisman in his pocket and ran to the middle of the room.

74
00:05:43.926 --> 00:05:50.335
"There's nowhere to run, boy!" Morb laughed nastily.

75
00:05:50.336 --> 00:05:57.950
Zann was desperately trying to think of a plan when Wyssa stepped toward him. "Take my hand, Zann," she said.

76
00:05:57.951 --> 00:06:00.373
"What?" he blurted out.

77
00:06:00.374 --> 00:06:03.722
Wyssa grabbed Zann's hand and yanked him toward the corner.

78
00:06:03.723 --> 00:06:07.209
Morb watched her suspiciously. "What are you—"

79
00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:13.388
A thunderous humming sound drowned out Morb's voice, and a glowing ring of light appeared in the room.

80
00:06:13.389 --> 00:06:18.384
As Zann peered into the swirling vortex, he nearly lost his balance.

81
00:06:18.385 --> 00:06:23.383
"Whatever you do, don't let go of my hand," warned Wyssa.

82
00:06:23.384 --> 00:06:30.267
With that, she pulled Zann into the wormhole.

